Vajra,
(1) n. of a samādhi: Mvy 〔516〕 (var. Vajropama, q.v.): ŚsP 〔1416.1〕;
(2) n. of a future Buddha: Gv 〔441.26〕.

vajraka,
(1) adj. (from vajra; in Skt. only with taila, a medicinal oil), diamantine, hard, fig.: adhyāśayair vajrakaiḥ LV 〔216.4〕 (vs);
(2) n. of a guhyaka (cf. Pali Vajira, n. of a yakkha): Mmk 〔532.16〕 (vs);
(3) n. of a mountain: Divy 〔450.10, 13〕; 〔455.29〕; 〔456.1〕;
(4) m., n. of a muhūrta: Divy 〔643.13〕; in 〔644.15〕 written varjanakaḥ.

Vajraśrī,
(1) n. of a ‘gandharva maid’: Kv 〔4.15〕;
(2) f., n. of a number of lokadhātus: Dbh 〔99.17〕.

Vajrasena,
(1) n. of a merchant, former birth of Śākyamuni; in the story of Śyāmā: Mv 〔ii.166.19 ff.〕;
(2) n. of one or two Bodhisattvas: Kv 〔1.8〕; Mmk 〔576.18〕.
